<title>USA: TABLE - Riviera Holdings Q2 net slips.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Riviera Holdings Q2 net slips.</headline>
<dateline>LAS VEGAS 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>RIVIERA HOLDINGS CORP</p>
<p>				   3 Mos ended 6/30  6 Mos ended 6/30</p>
<p>				1997	  1996	1997	 1996</p>
<p>REVENUES:</p>
<p> Casino		  $19,332     $20,217   $38,134    $40,382</p>
<p> Rooms		    10,930	10,514    21,424     21,771</p>
<p> Food and beverage     5,787	 6,215    11,248     12,043</p>
<p> Entertainment	   5,327	 5,493    10,759     11,247</p>
<p> Other		     2,670	 2,398     5,241	4,752</p>
<p>			    44,046	44,837    86,806     90,195</p>
<p>Less promotional</p>
<p>  allowances	     3,424	 3,285     6,703	6,922</p>
<p> Net revenues	   40,622	41,552    80,103     83,273</p>
<p> NET INCOME		2,019	 2,145     3,003	4,616</p>
<p> NET EPS		    0.39	  0.42	0.58	 0.90</p>
<p> WGTD AVG SHRS	   5,208	 5,132     5,212	5,132</p>
<p>		  (In thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: EBITDA margin increased to 20.6% of net revenues from 19.1% last year.</p>
<p>Net income fell while EBITDA increased due to 30% increase in depreciation from $2.0 million in Q2 1996 to $2.6 million in 1997.  The increase in depreciation is due to the $16.5 million of capital expenditures for rooms refurbishing and other upgrades to the Riviera in the 12 months ended June 30, 1997, which are amortized over seven years, the company said.</p>
</text>
